#, no-c-format
msgid "Minuet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "Welcome to &minuet;: the software for music education. &minuet; aims at supporting students and teachers in many aspects of music education, such as ear training, first-sight reading, solfa, scales, rhythm, harmony, and improvisation. &minuet; makes extensive use of &MIDI; capabilities to provide a full-fledged set of features regarding volume, tempo, and pitch changes, which makes &minuet; a valuable tool for both novice and experienced musicians."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "Welcome to &minuet;: the software for music education. It is built around short exercises that let you listen, respond, and test your progress without leaving the app."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "The app currently covers melodic ear training, rhythm recognition, clapping exercises, and singing exercises. The same exercise can often be practiced in more than one way, which is why the interface first asks whether you want to hear and identify, read and clap, or read and sing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; features a rich set of ear training's exercises and new ones can be <link linkend=\"creating-exercises\"> seamlessly added</link> in order to extend its functionalities and adapt it to several music education contexts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; home screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet;'s UI components"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &minuet; home screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "The home page is intentionally minimal. Use the navigation drawer to move to the settings page, the about page, or a category of exercises."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "In the next two sections - <link linkend=\"starting-minuet\">Starting &minuet;</link> and <link linkend=\"minuet-exercises\">&minuet; Exercises</link> - we will provide you the required steps to get &minuet; up and running."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &minuet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "The normal flow is simple: start &minuet;, choose an exercise, pick a practice mode, then work through a question or a test run."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can start &minuet; from the application launcher. Open the global menu by clicking on the application launcher icon on the system tray at the bottom left of your screen. This will raise a menu. Move your cursor up the menu to the <menuchoice><guimenu>Applications</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Education</guisubmenu> <guisubmenu>Miscellaneous</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>&minuet; (Music Education Software)</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item from the global menu or with <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo> and entering <command>minuet</command> into the input field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting &minuet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start &minuet; from the application launcher or from a terminal by running <command>minuet</command>. When the app opens, the home page shows a single prompt: <guilabel>Choose an exercise</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet;'s user interface entails three major components:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid "Browse and choose exercises"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "The exercise browser groups topics by subject. Use the drawer or the category list to reach chords, intervals, rhythm, or scales. The browser updates itself from the installed exercise specification files, so the visible hierarchy reflects the exercises that are currently available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigation Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; exercise browser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; Exercises and Workflow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allows for navigating in &minuet;'s exercise categories and selecting a particular exercise. The Navigation Menu is dynamically created based upon exercises specification files as described in <link linkend=\"creating-exercises\">Creating Exercises</link>. &minuet;'s exercises are grouped according to classes such as intervals, scales, and chords."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "The exercise browser in &minuet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keyboard View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exhibits &MIDI; <parameter>note on</parameter> events being sequenced by a &MIDI; file or by an exercise execution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each exercise entry has a title and a short description. Some categories lead directly to an exercise, while others expand into subcategories. The list is not fixed in code: new exercise files are merged into the hierarchy automatically when &minuet; starts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exercise View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "Presents, for a given exercise, buttons for controlling exercise presentation and a set of exercise's possible answers. An exercise run begins by clicking the <guibutton>Start Quest</guibutton> button. A randomly selected interval/chord/scale is played by &minuet; and then the student is expected to pick up an answer among the ones shown in the answer's grid. &minuet; always present - as a white small circle in Keyboard View - the first note of selected interval/scale or the root note of selected chord. By hovering a possible answer, &minuet; highlights its corresponding visual representation in Keyboard View. The remaining notes of the hovered answer are presented as small circles whose colors are the same of hovered answer's button. The student can hear the exercise again by clicking the <guibutton>Play Question</guibutton> button, click the chosen answer button, or get the right answer by clicking the <guibutton>Give Up</guibutton> button. A new run of the same exercise can be started by pressing <guibutton>Stop Quest</guibutton> button and pressing again the <guibutton>New Question</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "Practice modes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "When you open an exercise, &minuet; asks how you want to practice it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet;'s exercises are defined in exercise specification files, written in &JSON; format:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; practice mode chooser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"exercises\": [\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"name\": \"Intervals\",\n"
"      \"root\": \"21..104\",\n"
"      \"playMode\": \"scale\",\n"
"      \"children\": [\n"
"        {\n"
"          \"name\": \"Ascending Melodic Intervals\",\n"
"          \"children\": [\n"
"            {\n"
"              \"name\": \"Seconds\",\n"
"              \"options\": [\n"
"                {\n"
"                  \"name\": \"Minor Second\",\n"
"                  \"sequenceFromRoot\": \"1\"\n"
"                },\n"
"                {\n"
"                  \"name\": \"Major Second\",\n"
"                  \"sequenceFromRoot\": \"2\"\n"
"                }\n"
"              ]\n"
"            }\n"
"          ]\n"
"        }\n"
"      ]\n"
"    }\n"
"  ]\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "The practice mode chooser in &minuet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet;'s exercise specification files contain one top-level &JSON; object featuring the <parameter>exercises</parameter> array. Such an array defines a hierarchical structure of exercises, grouped by categories. Every category/exercise has a name. Category &JSON; objects contain a property named <parameter>children</parameter>, which describes the subcategories/exercises entailed by such a category. Exercise &JSON; objects contain a property named <parameter> options</parameter>, which defines the possible answers for such an exercise. In each exercise run, &minuet; randomly selects one answer among the possible ones and the student is expected to click the answer's button which corresponds to the selected answer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two broad practice paths:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "Any (sub)category may define a <parameter>root</parameter> parameter to specify the range from which the initial interval/chord/scale's note will be randomly chosen for all exercises in this category. Such range corresponds to standards &MIDI; note numbers and follows the format <parameter>&lt;min-value&gt;..&lt;max-value&gt;</parameter>. The example presented above uses all keyboard range as possible root notes (21..104). The <parameter>playMode</parameter> parameter indicates how possible answers should be played: as a <parameter>scale</parameter> (one note after the other) or as a <parameter>chord</parameter> (all notes ringing out simultaneously)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Hear and identify</guilabel> plays the exercise and asks you to choose the answer from the available options. This is the main flow for melodic ear training."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Read and clap</guilabel> is shown for rhythm exercises. <guilabel>Read and sing</guilabel> is shown for melodic exercises that accept vocal input, such as intervals and scales."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each exercise's option defines a name and the sequence of notes which should be played from the root note randomly selected in each exercise run. Such sequence of notes is defined as relative distances from the root note, describing the interval each note forms in conjunction with the root note. For example, for a major scale, the sequence of notes is <quote>2 4 5 7 9 11 12</quote>, which respectively denotes the <quote>whole whole half whole whole whole half</quote> major scale structure. The <parameter>sequenceFromRoot</parameter> parameter may contain any notes in length. Also, &minuet;'s core ensures that only answers whose all notes lies within keyboard range are randomly selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "The practice choice changes the input mode, not the underlying exercise category. That means you can use the same exercise data for listening, clapping, or singing work depending on the topic."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "To provide a better infrastructure for organizing a large set of exercise specification files, &minuet;'s core supports the use of several specification files, which are automatically merged to compose the final exercise hierarchy presented in the Navigation Menu. Exercises are correctly merged as long as different specification files use the same (sub)category name when defining exercises. For now, &minuet;'s provides no &GUI; for creating exercise specifications so that you must manually create such &JSON; files. &minuet;'s exercise specification files may be installed system-wide or locally in the <filename class=\"directory\">minuet/exercises/</filename> folder located in <userinput><command>qtpaths</command> <option>--paths GenericDataLocation</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Melodic ear training"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "Melodic exercises follow the classic Minuet flow: the app plays a question, shows answer choices, and lets you replay the prompt if you need to hear it again. This manual mode is used for intervals, scales, and chords when you choose <guilabel>Hear and identify</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; chord exercise in manual mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "A chord exercise in manual mode in &minuet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "The exercise page gives you the controls you need for a single question or a longer test run:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>New Question</guibutton> starts another question."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Play Question</guibutton> repeats the current prompt."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Give Up</guibutton> reveals the answer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Start Test</guibutton> begins a scored sequence of questions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Stop Test</guibutton> ends the test run."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "In melodic exercises, the answer buttons and the keyboard or staff view stay aligned, so you can see how each candidate maps to the notes being played."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Chord exercises use the same manual workflow, but the prompt is played as a chord instead of a melodic sequence. &minuet; plays the chord, shows the root note on the keyboard and staff, and asks you to choose one chord quality from the available answers. The chord catalog includes triads, inversions, suspended chords, seventh chords, ninth chords, eleventh chords, and mixed chord sets such as <guilabel>Lots of chords</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use <guibutton>Play Question</guibutton> to hear the chord again before answering. In test mode, &minuet; scores the sequence using the configured number of exercises from the settings page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rhythm and clapping"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rhythm exercises focus on timing rather than pitch. In the clapping mode, &minuet; listens to your microphone input and compares the onsets to the target pattern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; clapping exercise"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid "A rhythm clapping exercise in &minuet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "The clapping view shows the rhythm pattern cards, an input level meter, and a <guibutton>Calibrate Silence</guibutton> action. The count-in happens before recording starts, so you can settle into the tempo before the exercise listens for claps."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use the rhythm practice to work on:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "recognizing simple rhythm figures by ear;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "matching your claps to the beat;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "staying inside the configured timing tolerance."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "Singing exercises"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "Singing exercises use the microphone to compare what you sing with the target pitch content. The same practice screen is used for both interval and scale work, but the target and feedback change with the chosen exercise."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "For interval exercises, &minuet; plays the root note and asks you to sing the requested interval relative to it. For scale exercises, the app presents a scale or mode and expects you to sing the notes in sequence while staying on pitch and on beat."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; singing interval exercise"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "A singing interval exercise in &minuet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; singing scale exercise"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> stable6
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet;'s ear training chord exercises"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "A singing scale exercise in &minuet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid "The singing view shows the note targets, pitch and onset feedback, a live input meter, and a <guibutton>Calibrate Silence</guibutton> action. &minuet; also counts in before the first note, so you can start on the correct beat. The scale view extends the same feedback to longer sequences, which makes it useful for practicing melodic memory in addition to pitch matching."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid "Singing exercises are influenced by several settings:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Voice class</guilabel> selects the expected vocal range."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Pitch tolerance</guilabel> controls how far from the target pitch a sung note may be."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Timing tolerance</guilabel> controls how much rhythmic drift is accepted for claps."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "The settings page is split into four sections: <guilabel>Practice</guilabel>, <guilabel>Sound</guilabel>, <guilabel>Microphone</guilabel>, and <guilabel>Advanced</guilabel>. The first three sections keep the beginner controls visible. The advanced section stays collapsed until you open it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; basic settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "The basic settings page in &minuet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid "The visible settings cover the controls most users need day to day:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Exercise speed</guilabel> sets the tempo in beats per minute."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Number of rhythm patterns</guilabel> controls the size of rhythm practice sets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Number of exercises</guilabel> sets the length of a test run."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Volume</guilabel> adjusts playback loudness."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Instrument</guilabel> selects the melodic sound used for ear training."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Voice class</guilabel> selects the target singing range."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "The microphone section also includes short helper descriptions for the tolerance and calibration controls. Those descriptions explain when to tighten the tolerance and when to recalibrate silence."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet; advanced settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "The advanced settings section in &minuet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced settings expose detection algorithms and thresholds for difficult microphones or noisy rooms. Use them when the default detection behavior is not enough. The section is collapsed by default and includes a <guibutton>Reset to Defaults</guibutton> button so you can restore the factory values after experimenting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "The advanced section includes separate groups for clapping detection and singing detection. Typical controls include onset method, onset threshold, input gate, minimum onset strength, silence level, pitch method, scoring mode, pitch confidence, and stable pitch frames."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating new &minuet;'s exercises"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "&minuet;'s exercises are defined in &JSON; specification files. The app loads all available files at startup and merges them into the visible exercise tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"exercises\": [\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"name\": \"Intervals\",\n"
"      \"root\": \"29..69\",\n"
"      \"playMode\": \"scale\",\n"
"      \"userMessage\": \"Hear the interval and choose your answer\",\n"
"      \"numberOfSelectedOptions\": 1,\n"
"      \"_icon\": \"minuet-intervals-symbolic.svg\",\n"
"      \"children\": [\n"
"        {\n"
"          \"name\": \"Ascending melodic intervals\",\n"
"          \"and-tags\": [\"interval\", \"ascending\"],\n"
"          \"children\": [\n"
"            {\n"
"              \"name\": \"Seconds\",\n"
"              \"or-tags\": [\"2\"],\n"
"              \"description\": \"Practice identifying ascending melodic seconds by ear.\"\n"
"            }\n"
"          ]\n"
"        }\n"
"      ]\n"
"    }\n"
"  ]\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid "The top-level object contains an <parameter>exercises</parameter> array. Each item in that array is either a category or an exercise leaf. Categories use <parameter>children</parameter> to define the next level of the tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "Useful fields include:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>name</parameter> gives every node its visible label."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>root</parameter> limits the note range used to generate the prompt."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>playMode</parameter> selects scale, chord, or rhythm playback."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>userMessage</parameter> customizes the instruction shown to the user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>numberOfSelectedOptions</parameter> controls how many answers may be correct."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>_icon</parameter> sets the icon shown in the drawer and exercise browser."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>and-tags</parameter> and <parameter>or-tags</parameter> help group and filter related nodes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>description</parameter> gives the browser a short explanation for the node."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>options</parameter> describes answer choices for a leaf exercise."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>sequenceFromRoot</parameter> defines the note offsets for melodic answers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>template</parameter> is used by rhythm exercises to render notation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: index.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "The app merges files that share the same category names, so separate specification files can contribute to one visible hierarchy. Install them system-wide or place them in <filename class=\"directory\">minuet/exercises/</filename> under the generic data location returned by <userinput><command>qtpaths</command> <option>--paths GenericDataLocation</option></userinput>."
msgstr ""

